    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d303-a7">

                <pb facs="0366" n="1100" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1100"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 7 in No. 151.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Peirce to Mr.
                            Rawicz.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-05"><hi rendition="#italic">October 5,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have telegraphed you to-day as follows:
                    “Was Yablkowski’s passport viséed to enter Russia?”</p>
                <p>If it is possible for you to obtain this information you will please do so with
                    as little delay as possible, informing me also, if you can, by what Russian
                    consul or other officer such visé was affixed to his passport.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herbert H. D. Peirce</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
